&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Lauren, Senior Manager of Customer Success at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I&#39;m looking for a Customer Success Manager to join our Mid-Market, APAC or EMEA team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the success of a dedicated portfolio of roughly 40-60 Mid-Market customers — acting as their strategic advisor from onboarding through long-term adoption, and driving commercial outcomes across your book of business. You&#39;ll partner closely with Account Management, Technical Support, Product, Solutions, and Engineering to help customers realize real value throughout their lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t need you to be a marketing expert or a deeply technical one. We need someone who&#39;s an expert at asking the right questions — someone who digs until they find the real problem, not just the reported one, and who can influence a customer to make progress and move through blockers. You&#39;ll be curious and eager to understand our app well enough to take a customer&#39;s use case and turn our features into outcomes that matter to them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity about the business behind the customer:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re genuinely interested in how companies operate and enjoy learning your customers&#39; industries and goals. You ask about the &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; behind a request before recommending a solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trusted advisor, not ticket-taker:&lt;/strong&gt; You build relationships that turn you into a strategic partner rather than someone who simply answers questions. You have well-formed opinions about customer experience and aren&#39;t shy about sharing them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership of commercial outcomes:&lt;/strong&gt; You see CS as a value and growth engine. You take ownership of outcomes across your book and naturally look for opportunities to create more value, partnering with AM on retention and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort in ambiguity:&lt;/strong&gt; You thrive on complex, open-ended customer challenges — bringing together business context, technical understanding, and creativity to solve them. You&#39;re calm under pressure, highly organized, and able to juggle competing priorities across a full portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-forward thinking:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re comfortable using AI tools to improve your own productivity and your customers&#39; outcomes, and you bring a growth mindset toward experimenting with new AI-powered ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a dedicated portfolio of ~40-60 Mid-Market customers as their strategic partner across the full customer lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead onboarding — running kickoffs and milestone check-ins, and guiding customers to their first measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of each customer&#39;s goals and translate them into measurable, mutual success plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide proactive, consultative guidance through regular strategic touchpoints and value-driven conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor customer health, spot adoption trends, and address risks before they impact success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Management to support retention and expansion, and coordinate with Technical Support, Product, Solutions, and Engineering when deeper expertise is needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own escalations end to end — from identification through resolution — keeping customers informed and confident throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for your customers internally by sharing product feedback and influencing improvements to the customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive AI adoption across your portfolio — coaching customers on AI-powered solutions and modeling what AI-native Customer Success looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the broader CS organization by sharing best practices, improving playbooks, and participating in webinars and enablement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years as a Customer Success Manager for technical products, in a SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating with software developers in a technical capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opinionated about customer experience — you should have well-formed views in order to give customers strategic advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in French, Russian, and/or Spanish (we are prioritizing multilingual candidates for this role)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Australia, New Zealand, United Kingdom or Ireland&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience designing lifecycle messages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. The salary for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$80,000 USD&lt;/strong&gt; (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we&#39;re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers#:~:text=our%20collective%20success.-,BENEFITS,-Our%C2%A0&quot;&gt;See full benefits here →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No gotchas, no trick questions - just a clear, human process designed to help both of us make an informed decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute video call with Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;45-minute video call with Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;45-minute Homework Review Call + feedback with potential team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All final candidates will be asked to complete a background check and employment verifications as part of our pre-employment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; recognizes the stifling impact of systemic injustice on diverse communities. We commit to using our influence to increase inclusion and equity within the tech industry. We strive to build an inclusive team culture, implement bias-free hiring practices, and develop community partnerships to expand our global impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zoom is the only video conference platform that we use, virtual interviews will be conducted using the video capability (i.e., not via the chat), and offers will be extended in writing on official &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; letterhead. Please be vigilant in all of your job search activity, and if you have any questions please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:jobs@customer.io&quot;&gt;jobs@customer.io&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Join us!&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers/&quot;&gt;careers page&lt;/a&gt; for more information about why you should &lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/about/&quot;&gt;come work with us!&lt;/a&gt; We believe in empathy, transparency, responsibility, and, yes, a little awkwardness. If you&#39;re excited by what you read — apply now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Diep Nguyen, VP of Finance here at &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I&#39;m looking for a Director, GTM Finance to own our go-to-market P&amp;amp;L end-to-end as we scale from $100M+ ARR today to $1B+ ARR in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring for strategic finance horsepower first: someone who builds models from a blank page, challenges assumptions, and earns trust with senior executives. Deep GTM fluency matters just as much — but for a strong finance generalist, that business partnership often shows up in the work rather than the title. You&#39;ll own our GTM P&amp;amp;L spanning Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success, and build the team behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re an AI-forward company: this role requires someone energized by using AI to reinvent how finance operates, not someone who merely tolerates the tools we hand them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial rigor over title-matching&lt;/strong&gt; — we care more about how you&#39;ve built and defended models than whether &quot;GTM Finance&quot; was ever your title.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI as genuine practice, not a buzzword&lt;/strong&gt; — we want concrete stories of AI changing an outcome, not familiarity with the tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership from day one&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;ll build and lead a team, not just execute analysis handed to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Directness with data&lt;/strong&gt; — you challenge top-down assumptions with account-level evidence, even in uncomfortable conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GTM P&amp;amp;L end-to-end — revenue, gross margin, and opex across Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success — not just a spend-efficiency lens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive unit economics and the growth funnel model — CAC, LTV/CAC, payback, magic number, and cohort/retention analysis across self-serve and sales-assisted motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the ARR roll-forward, bookings, and revenue forecasting — auditable, reconcilable, and independently stress-tested against top-down assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and RevOps on capacity planning, deal economics, and pricing — protecting margin and ARR quality without slowing deal velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the monthly/quarterly GTM reporting package for the exec team and Board, with variance analysis that explains root cause.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-enabled finance workflows and build the GTM finance team as &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; scales past $250M+ ARR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, or related roles at complex, scaled orgs; a first-principles modeler who builds from a blank page rather than inheriting assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep GTM business-partnering experience with Sales, Marketing, or Customer Success — regardless of whether &quot;GTM Finance&quot; was ever the title&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with subscription/SaaS metrics (ARR, NRR, CAC, LTV) or able to get there fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concrete, demonstrated track record driving AI adoption in finance workflows — not just familiarity with the tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people leader — has managed and developed finance professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills (with experience using Snowflake a plus) and experience with planning/GTM systems (NetSuite, Salesforce, Gong, Drivetrain)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or related field; MBA a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$200K–$255K USD&lt;/strong&gt; (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we’re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers#:~:text=our%20collective%20success.-,BENEFITS,-Our%C2%A0&quot;&gt;See full benefits here →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No gotchas, no trick questions - just a clear, human process designed to help both of us make an informed decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiter Screen (30 min)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring Manager Screen (45 min)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two Cross-functional conversations with team members (30 min each)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Case study + Case Review Panel with team (45 min)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All final candidates will be asked to complete a background check and employment verifications as part of our pre-employment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; recognizes the stifling impact of systemic injustice on diverse communities. We commit to using our influence to increase inclusion and equity within the tech industry. We strive to build an inclusive team culture, implement bias-free hiring practices, and develop community partnerships to expand our global impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zoom is the only video conference platform that we use, virtual interviews will be conducted using the video capability (i.e., not via the chat), and offers will be extended in writing on official &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; letterhead. Please be vigilant in all of your job search activity, and if you have any questions please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:jobs@customer.io&quot;&gt;jobs@customer.io&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Join us!&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers/&quot;&gt;careers page&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about why you should&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/about/&quot;&gt;come work with us!&lt;/a&gt; We believe in empathy, transparency, responsibility, and, yes, a little awkwardness. If you’re excited by what you read — apply now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Caitlin, Senior Manager, Technical Support at &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I&#39;m looking for an Email Deliverability Specialist to join our deliverability program within Technical Support. You&#39;ll help customers reach the inbox by diagnosing sending issues, advising on best practices, and guiding senders through an email ecosystem that keeps changing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be one of several deliverability experts on a team that shares knowledge across Technical Support, so your work reaches well beyond your own queue. You&#39;ll partner with Customer Success, Technical Support, and Engineering: taking customer calls, equipping CSMs for customer conversations, working through complex technical cases alongside Engineering, and turning what you see in tickets into documentation, training, and better processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll thrive here if you think about the health of the whole program, enjoy improving how work gets done, and are equally comfortable digging into a detailed case and having a direct conversation with a customer about acceptable use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathy and curiosity:&lt;/strong&gt; You approach every customer with patience and a desire to dig deeper, especially when a conversation gets uncomfortable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity:&lt;/strong&gt; You explain complex technical concepts simply and help others do the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; You build strong partnerships across Support, Customer Success, and Engineering, and you treat customer outcomes as a shared goal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thinking at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; You look at how we do things today and see what could work better for the whole organization, then you help make it happen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous learning:&lt;/strong&gt; You stay ahead of evolving standards and see change as a chance to improve how we work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted deliverability advisor to customers, handling complex cases through to full resolution and leading customer calls when a conversation needs it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit sender setup and monitor reputation across IPs and domains, using authentication (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) and BIMI, DNS configuration, and provider tools like Google Postmaster Tools, Yahoo Sender Hub, and Microsoft SNDS to diagnose blocklists, spam traps, and engagement drops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work through highly technical issues with Engineering, taking ownership of the investigation first and sharing trends from customer cases with Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify acceptable use policy violations and spam complaints, hold clear and direct conversations with customers about compliance, and keep up with evolving standards (Gmail and Yahoo sender requirements, CAN-SPAM, GDPR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip CSMs and Technical Support with the knowledge to handle deliverability conversations, through coaching, documentation, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve processes, tools, and one-to-many resources, such as help content, Academy course and proactive customer guidance, so deliverability support scales across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience in email deliverability at a mid-size or large ESP, B2B SaaS company, or marketing automation platform, with exposure to deliverability at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of email authentication (SPF, DKIM, DMARC, BIMI) and infrastructure (SMTP, MTAs, DNS), with the technical comfort to work through complex issues with Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with provider data feeds (Google Postmaster Tools, Yahoo Sender Hub, Microsoft SNDS) and third-party deliverability monitoring tools like Everest, MXToolbox, or similar, and the analytical skill to turn bounce, engagement, and blocklist data into clear recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of email compliance and acceptable use standards, and comfort having direct conversations with customers who are sending outside of them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving processes, documentation, or training that help a support or deliverability team scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, including comfort leading customer calls and simplifying technical concepts for any audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in the United States or Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: participation in deliverability communities (M3AAWG, ESPC, or similar) and experience partnering with Customer Success teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is $102,000 - $110,000 USD (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we&#39;re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers#:~:text=our%20collective%20success.-,BENEFITS,-Our%C2%A0&quot;&gt;See full benefits here →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No gotchas, no trick questions - just a clear, human process designed to help both of us make an informed decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute video call with a Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;45-minute video call with the Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;60 minute Case Study Review call with Cross-Functional Partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute video call with potential Team Member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 minute final video call with Senior Leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All final candidates will be asked to complete a background check and employment verifications as part of our pre-employment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; recognizes the stifling impact of systemic injustice on diverse communities. We commit to using our influence to increase inclusion and equity within the tech industry. We strive to build an inclusive team culture, implement bias-free hiring practices, and develop community partnerships to expand our global impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zoom is the only video conference platform that we use, virtual interviews will be conducted using the video capability (i.e., not via the chat), and offers will be extended in writing on official &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; letterhead. Please be vigilant in all of your job search activity, and if you have any questions please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:jobs@customer.io&quot;&gt;jobs@customer.io&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Join us!&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers/&quot;&gt;careers page&lt;/a&gt; for more information about why you should &lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/about/&quot;&gt;come work with us!&lt;/a&gt; We believe in empathy, transparency, responsibility, and, yes, a little awkwardness. If you&#39;re excited by what you read — apply now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hi, I&#39;m Paul, VP of Engineering at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re always looking for thoughtful, driven Engineering Managers to add to our org. Some of our teams are building customer-facing product and workflows; others keep our distributed systems reliable, observable, and ready to scale. Whichever kind of problem energizes you, if you lead people well, hold a high technical bar, and drive work to completion without waiting to be handed a plan, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies—from scrappy startups to global brands—use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data—what people do or don&#39;t do inside a web or mobile app. Under the hood: Go, React, and AI help us ship fast and scale with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we value&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You set direction and see initiatives through. You create clarity when things are murky and set the path forward rather than waiting for one to be defined, and you&#39;re motivated by impact—not just intention. You hold yourself and your team accountable to shipping, not just staying busy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leaders who can do both.&lt;/strong&gt; You operate at the strategic level and stay close to the technical work. You can align stakeholders on a plan and earn your engineers&#39; respect in the same day—you don&#39;t choose between vision and execution, you hold both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A drive to execute through resistance.&lt;/strong&gt; Competing priorities, skeptical stakeholders, tired teams—you&#39;ve moved work forward anyway. You name the resistance, make the call, and own the milestones and the misses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An AI-first mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; AI is central to how you build and how you lead your team to build. You have a real, concrete point of view on AI-native development, you use agentic tooling yourself, and you bring it into how your squad operates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A healthy skepticism for &quot;the way things are done.&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; You bring rigor and pragmatism. Best practices matter—but never more than forward motion. You know when to build, when to buy, and when to wait—and you&#39;re comfortable making the call with incomplete information, then adjusting as you learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care deeply about our customers and their outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your squad to deliver real customer value by owning projects end to end—from planning through delivery, quality, and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution: set milestones, keep work moving through ambiguity and competing priorities, and&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;ship in small, observable increments rather than waiting for a release window&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make confident decisions when the path isn&#39;t obvious, and lead your team through them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the operating rhythm that helps your team move fastest, rather than defaulting to ceremony for its own sake&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure your squad&#39;s solutions are scalable, architecturally sound, flexible, and secure, with strong peer-review, QA, documentation, deployment, logging, and monitoring practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the work—jump into design reviews, architecture calls, and incidents rather than watching from a distance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct, timely, and specific coaching, and create meaningful development opportunities for your direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation as required, supporting the reliability of the systems you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, onboard, and manage performance so the right people are in place to hit your squad&#39;s goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring an AI-native perspective—use AI tools to accelerate the team&#39;s velocity and help everyone prototype faster and ship smarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across engineering and other departments to align efforts with customer success, and reach higher when our customers are having a bad day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing engineers at a SaaS company (B2B or B2C), ideally early-to-mid-stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving execution—concrete delivery outcomes with milestones, dates, and &quot;I drove&quot; ownership, especially in complex or fast-moving environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical background—you can hold your own in architecture conversations and design reviews, represent your squad&#39;s technical choices across the company, and you&#39;ve shipped real work recently enough to stay credible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with high autonomy and little prescribed structure—you create your own clarity and make difficult tradeoffs between competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI-native leadership—not just personal fluency, but bringing AI-first practices into how your team builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high-performing, inclusive, and collaborative teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise, and direct communication, both verbal and written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is $185,000-$215,000 USD (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we&#39;re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers#:~:text=our%20collective%20success.-,BENEFITS,-Our%C2%A0&quot;&gt;See full benefits here →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Process&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No gotchas, no trick questions - just a clear, human process designed to help both of us make an informed decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application&lt;/strong&gt; - We review everyone with care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiter Call (30 mins)&lt;/strong&gt; - Let&#39;s chat about what you&#39;re looking for, your leadership style, and how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Manager Interview (60 mins)&lt;/strong&gt; - Deep dive into your experience leading teams, your technical philosophy, and how you think about building organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Partner Interview (30 mins)&lt;/strong&gt; - Explore your leadership style, management philosophy, and approach to supporting high-performing teams with our engineering people partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Interview (60 mins)&lt;/strong&gt; - Engage in a collaborative system design conversation focused on scaling challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take-Home Assignment&lt;/strong&gt; - Submit a short written retrospective on a project you’ve led as an Engineering Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retrospective Review Call (60 mins)&lt;/strong&gt; - We’ll use your written submission as the foundation for a deeper conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All final candidates will be asked to complete a background check and employment verifications as part of our pre-employment process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Rosie, Events Team Manager here at &lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I am looking for an Events Marketing Manager to own our in-person events across EMEA. You&#39;ll lead live field events, hosted customer and prospect experiences, and sponsored conferences across the region, and run our monthly EMEA webinar. You&#39;ll partner closely with Demand Gen, Content, Design, Partnerships, and EMEA Sales to create events that feel polished, thoughtful, and unmistakably &quot;us&quot; - tailored to EMEA markets rather than a copy-paste of NA programming. You&#39;ll ramp alongside our Events Manager, who currently supports the region, and take full ownership of EMEA within your first 90 days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role includes 15%+ travel for EMEA field events, conferences, and onsite support.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human-centered experiences.&lt;/strong&gt; You create events that feel thoughtful, relevant, and genuinely useful - built for EMEA audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative energy.&lt;/strong&gt; You work smoothly across teams and time zones, and make alignment feel easy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insight-driven decisions.&lt;/strong&gt; You let data guide you while keeping the attendee experience at the center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Action with intention.&lt;/strong&gt; You move quickly, adapt gracefully, and learn from every event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational clarity.&lt;/strong&gt; You bring structure, calm, and consistency to fast-moving, cross-market work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event planning &amp;amp; coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the EMEA in-person events calendar - field events, hosted experiences, sponsored conferences, and activations across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Events Team and Demand Gen to define goals, audiences, formats, and success metrics specific to EMEA markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate EMEA sponsorships, speaking slots, and event formats against goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional partners to ensure every event feels cohesive with global campaigns while staying relevant to EMEA audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution &amp;amp; project management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day logistics: vendor coordination, timelines, run-of-show, speaker prep, and on-the-ground support for EMEA events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Content, Brand, Product Marketing, and Sales to develop compelling event assets and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee registration flows, pre-event communication, and the attendee experience from first touch to follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step in wherever needed to keep events running smoothly, calmly, and on-brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA webinars (about one per month)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run our monthly EMEA webinar end to end - topic and speaker selection, registration, promotion, and follow-up - timed and localized for a European audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Content and Product Marketing to adapt or build webinar content that lands with EMEA audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimize registration pages, forms, and workflows for EMEA campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audience growth &amp;amp; promotion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute multi-channel promotional plans across email, social, and partner channels for EMEA audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Demand Gen, Marketing Ops &amp;amp; Sales to ensure EMEA lead capture, routing, and follow-up happen correctly and quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage attendee communication throughout the event lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track EMEA event performance - pipeline, revenue, deal acceleration, and event engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share insights and recommendations to continually improve ROI and attendee experience across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation, templates, and repeatable workflows that make running EMEA events smoother and more scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with ops to ensure clean attribution and accurate reporting across systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; EMEA events and webinars run smoothly, predictably, and feel built for the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Attendance and engagement steadily increase across EMEA field events and webinars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; EMEA Sales and Marketing feel tightly connected and supported by event-driven pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharper insights:&lt;/strong&gt; You surface insights that help the program get sharper, smarter, and more efficient over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Better playbooks:&lt;/strong&gt; EMEA-specific playbooks, templates, and processes get better and help the team move faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a hands-on, highly organized marketer who loves building great experiences and understands how events translate into revenue. You&#39;re comfortable owning a region end to end - you stay grounded under pressure, thrive in a distributed environment, and enjoy the cross-market collaboration required to make EMEA events exceptional.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Based in the UK or Ireland&lt;/strong&gt; (London or Dublin ideal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years in event marketing within B2B SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running in-person events across formats (field events, hosted experiences, conferences), ideally across multiple EMEA markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running webinars, and real excitement about doing both: a busy in-person calendar plus about one webinar a month&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills - you juggle timelines, tasks, and teams (and time zones) with ease&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with Sales and supporting event-driven follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with marketing automation tools (&lt;a href=&quot;http://customer.io/&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, Marketo, etc.) and Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with webinar platforms (Livestorm, Zoom, Sequel) and event management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of lead capture, UTMs, and event pipeline attribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to partner with Rev/Marketing Ops to troubleshoot data flows and ensure clean reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with 15%+ travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is $93,000 - $110,000 USD (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we’re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://customer.io/careers#:~:text=our%20collective%20success.-,BENEFITS,-Our%C2%A0&quot;&gt;See full benefits here →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No gotchas, no trick questions - just a clear, human process designed to help both of us make an informed decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute video call with Recruiter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute video call with member of the Events team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30-minute video call with Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
