&lt;h3&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive. We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, my name is Matt Wensing, VP of Product &amp;amp; Design at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;, and I&#39;m looking for a Principal Product Designer. Principal Product Designer is the highest individual contributor design role at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;. This person shapes the design vision for the company and influences how design is practiced here — through their own craft, through the standards their work sets, and through the partnerships they build with product and engineering leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; is in a transformational moment: executing against a strong current product while redesigning what the product is and how it&#39;s experienced by a new generation of builders. This role has to straddle both — delivering quality and coherence in what exists today while driving the vision for where things go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a management role, but it&#39;s a leadership role in the fullest sense. Their influence is felt company-wide — in the product, in the culture, and in who we hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a fully formed point of view on how AI changes what software means — for the people who use it, the people who build it, and the agents that increasingly operate it. You have the conviction to put that view to work across a product and an organization. You lead through clarity and example, give candid feedback that improves the work, and operate with humility and curiosity even outside your own expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we value&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leads through clarity and example, not control.&lt;/strong&gt; You shape culture through your own practice — not top-down direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candid craft feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; You give feedback that improves the work, even when it&#39;s uncomfortable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Humility and curiosity.&lt;/strong&gt; You operate with openness, especially in areas outside your expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Amplifying others.&lt;/strong&gt; You raise the impact of people across the whole company — not just the design team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for craft.&lt;/strong&gt; You stay close to the work by choice, and that proximity is how you lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Some things you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape and communicate a design vision for &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&#39;s product as a whole&lt;/strong&gt; — the coherent, long-range picture of what excellent looks like for our customers, brought into rooms where product direction gets set&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive the strategic direction of Pluma&lt;/strong&gt;, our design system — architecture, evolution, deprecation decisions, and the principles that govern how it scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the gap between design intent and shipped product&lt;/strong&gt; — stay close enough to implementation to catch divergence, and fix it directly when code is the right tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for builder and developer audiences&lt;/strong&gt; — CLI-native flows, API-first onboarding, and interfaces built for people who type before they click&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the design of agentic and human-AI surfaces&lt;/strong&gt; across the product — develop the philosophy and advocate for the standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with product and engineering leadership on product strategy&lt;/strong&gt; — bring design into the conversation before direction is set, not after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and advocate for &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&#39;s AI product design philosophy&lt;/strong&gt; as a framework the whole team builds from&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead design review for major initiatives&lt;/strong&gt; and bring accountability for quality and coherence across what ships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Staff designers&lt;/strong&gt; through direct mentorship, critique, and the clarity of your own example&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to hiring and calibration&lt;/strong&gt; — assess candidates with conviction and help the team develop a shared language for what excellent looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years of product design experience&lt;/strong&gt; with a portfolio demonstrating design vision and organizational impact, not just individual craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of &lt;strong&gt;shaping design direction at the company level&lt;/strong&gt; — influenced what gets built and why, not just how it looks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Designed for developer and builder audiences&lt;/strong&gt; — CLI, API-first onboarding, or infrastructure-native products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developed point of view on AI and agentic product design&lt;/strong&gt; — has shipped AI-native interfaces and can articulate a philosophy on interaction models for agentic and delegated use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contributed to a design system at the strategic level&lt;/strong&gt; — shaped what it should be and shouldn&#39;t be, and advocated for those decisions over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operates with influence without authority&lt;/strong&gt; — track record of aligning product, engineering, and exec leadership around a design direction without a management title&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Has raised the craft bar at an organizational level&lt;/strong&gt; — through critique culture, standards, and the example others internalize&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive-level communication&lt;/strong&gt; — connects design decisions to customer impact, product differentiation, and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2B SaaS depth&lt;/strong&gt; — understands complex, data-heavy products and has opinions about where the interaction model breaks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. The starting salary for this role is &lt;strong&gt;$245k-$276k USD&lt;/strong&gt;, depending on experience and subject to market-rate adjustment. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know our people are what make us great, and we&#39;re committed to taking great care of them. Our inclusive benefits package supports your well-being and growth, including &lt;strong&gt;100% coverage of medical, dental, vision, mental health, and supplemental insurance premiums for you and your family&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer &lt;strong&gt;16 weeks of paid parental leave, unlimited PTO&lt;/strong&gt;, stipends for remote work and wellness, a professional development budget, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
