&lt;p&gt;Hi, I&#39;m Paul, VP of Engineering at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re looking for a staff engineer to set technical direction for the systems that move billions of messages a day. This isn&#39;t a role about shipping more, faster. It&#39;s about deciding what gets built, where the architecture needs to go next, and raising the ceiling for the engineers around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 9,000 companies — from scrappy startups to global brands — use our platform to send billions of emails, push notifications, in-app messages, and SMS every day. &lt;a href=&quot;http://Customer.io&quot;&gt;Customer.io&lt;/a&gt; powers automated communication that people actually want to receive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help teams send smarter, more relevant messages using real-time behavioral data. Under the hood: Go, React, Ember and AI help us ship fast and scale with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Value&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership at company scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You take on the problems nobody has claimed yet — the ones that span squads, have no obvious owner, and would quietly cost us a year if left alone. You either solve them or get leadership aligned to.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineers with product taste&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You think like a user, not just an engineer. You connect architectural decisions to what customers actually experience, and you can explain that connection to people who don&#39;t write Go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A healthy skepticism for &quot;the way things are done&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You retire practices that have outlived their usefulness, including ones you helped build. Best practices matter — but never more than forward motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Force multiplication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your best quarter isn&#39;t measured by what you shipped. It&#39;s measured by what the department can now do that it couldn&#39;t before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the technical direction of our distributed messaging systems in Go — making the high-level architectural calls on mission-critical services where scale, cost, and reliability are all in tension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on ambiguous, high-stakes problems that cross squad and function boundaries, and drive them to a decision when the right answer isn&#39;t obvious to anyone yet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build consensus on contested technical questions across teams, and communicate the tradeoffs clearly enough that senior leadership can act on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the department&#39;s bar — set quality and design standards, mentor senior engineers, and turn what you know into frameworks and documentation other teams can use without you in the room&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive engineering process and tooling improvements that span multiple squads, not just your own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation as required, supporting the reliability of the systems you build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview and calibrate against our career ladder, giving honest, evidence-based assessments of candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI agents to make multi-file changes by scoping the work, writing the prompt, and verifying the output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years building scalable, distributed systems in Go (or similar statically typed languages), including several as the person others turned to on architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depth across multiple systems or domains, not just one — you&#39;ve been the recognized expert in more than one place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing for production reality: you quantify tradeoffs in throughput, cost, and reliability rather than picking a reasonable path and defending it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing observability and recovery as first-class concerns — metrics, alerting, rollback, backpressure, checkpointing — not logging added afterward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in cloud-native environments (AWS, GCP), with relational databases (we use MySQL) and a real understanding of performance tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of making other engineers better: mentorship, technical writing, design review, standards that outlasted your involvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias for action over perfection, and the judgment to know which decisions are worth slowing down for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in transparency. Starting salary for this role is $200,000 - $240,000 USD (or equivalent in local currency) depending on experience and subject to market rate adjustment. This role also carries a 10% annual bonus target. In addition to base salary, this role includes an equity grant in the form of stock options, so you share in the success you help build.&lt;/p&gt;
